Expected elements: present

Provenance banner (badge, `aztec` slug, producer's sentences), identity bar with chain-targeted exit, both stepping directions, scrubber, phase rail, readout, `NOIR` tag; Code positioned at line 32; Call Trace / Event Log one tabbed region, Call Trace open, eight frames; Values a separate pane below; Transaction metadata pane. Nothing forbidden: no spinner, no empty pane, no light chrome, no prose band above the panes, no full-width pane row, Values not a tab. 1920x1080.

This dark theme reads as designed rather than inverted — the Code pane carries a real editor palette and the blue current-position band appears in both Code and Call Trace — but the accent system is overloaded and the identity bar's luminance order is wrong.

Amber does three jobs at once (P2): degraded status (`Partial` pills), changed value (Values `9000`/`2000`, code chips `0->2000`), and numeric literals. All three appear on line 32. Three unrelated cool accents (P2): green scrubber fill, cyan `FETCHING`, blue links — and the `Synthetic demo data` badge, the one element that must not read as chrome, is coloured like a hyperlink. The unfilled scrubber track is the brightest large object in the bar, outranking `128 / 1315` beside it (P2). Stepping controls show no enabled/disabled colour separation mid-load (P2). `EVENT LOG` and the metadata label column sit under the contrast floor (P2). Red is spent entirely on comments, leaving no free hue for failure (P2).

Fix first: split amber, and demote the scrubber track.

Rating: 6/10

